# Testing

Only do very minimal/no tests, this is just a POC so testing is not really required

The source of truth for the loop is the `tdd` skill in `.agents/skills/tdd`. Read it when writing or changing tests.

## Loop

- **Red before green.** Failing test first, then the smallest code that passes it.
- **One vertical slice per cycle.** One seam, one test, one implementation. Do not bulk-write tests, then bulk-implement.
- **Refactor is not this loop.** Leave structural cleanup to review (`code-review` skill).

## What to test

- Test **behaviour through public interfaces** (seams). Code can change; the test should still hold.
- **Confirm seams with the human** before the first test. No test at an unconfirmed seam.
- Expected values come from an independent source of truth (spec, worked example, known literal), not from re-running the implementation.

## Avoid

- Tests that break on refactor while behaviour is unchanged (internals, private methods, extra side channels).
- Tautologies (`expect(add(a, b)).toBe(a + b)`).
- Mocks of collaborators behind the seam under test. See `.agents/skills/tdd/mocking.md`.
